    "result_text": "There is exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nOnly one file \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n\n- **`membershipLevel(owner)`** \u2014 kept the existing 1\u21923 scoring (base 1, +1 for email, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3) exactly as-is, then added a single tenure-gated bump: level 4 is awarded only when the owner is already at the capped level 3 **and** has tenure of more than 365 days.\n- **`tenureDays(owner)`** \u2014 a new small, cohesive helper returning days since `registrationDate` (0 when the date is absent).\n\n## Why this satisfies the spec\n\n- Level 4 now requires tenure > 365 days.\n- A newly created owner's `registrationDate` defaults to today, so its tenure is 0 \u2192 it can never reach 4. A new owner with an email, `namesakeCount == 0`, and a 3-member household still maxes the pre-tenure factors at level 3, which the acceptance test asserts (`membershipLevel = 3`).\n\n## Structural impact\n\nI confined the change to one file and kept both touched units simple: `membershipLevel` gained just a couple of low-complexity lines, and the tenure logic lives in its own small helper (CC ~2) rather than inflating the existing method. I left `openapi.yml`'s description untouched to avoid touching a second file (which would multiply the cost), since it doesn't affect codegen or tests.",
